''[[Cheers]]'' originally aired on [[NBC]] from September 30, 1982 to May 20, 1993. Over the series run, 275 original episodes aired, an average of around 25 episodes per season. In the early 1990s, 20 volumes of [[VHS]] cassettes were released; each had three half-hour episodes.<ref name=vhs>Hunt, Dennis. {{Deprecated archive|url=https://archive.today/20130201080758/http://pqasb.pqarchiver.com/latimes/access/60290220.html?FMT=ABS&FMTS=ABS:FT|title="Cheer Up! 'Cheers' Lives via Mail Order"}}. ''[[Los Angeles Times]]'' 14 May 1993: F18. Web. 1 June 2012. {{subscription required}}</ref> The whole series is available on multi-disc sets on [[DVD]], two to four per season. The series is also available on [[iTunes]], on [[Paramount+]] and Seasons 1–4 are on [[Hulu]]. Episodes aired on C4 and C4+1 on weekdays.

